### 6. Technical Specifications for Prototype Implementation

| Parameter | Value | Rationale |
|-----------|-------|-----------|
| Embedding dimension \(d\) | 768 | Matches base LLM hidden size |
| Max vertices \(|\mathcal{V}|\) | 10,000 | Document‑scale reasoning |
| Max hyperedges \(|\mathcal{E}|\) | 5,000 | Balance expressiveness & compute |
| Basis size \(K\) | 64 | Sufficient for micro‑level expansion |
| Chebyshev tolerance \(\delta\) | \(10^{-6}\) | Ensures backward error below machine epsilon |
| Merge threshold \(\tau_0\) | 0.7 | Empirically chosen |
| Merge diffusion offset \(\tau_{\text{diff}}\) | 0.2 | Encourages merging in diffusion regime |
| AP update rate \(\alpha_0\) | 0.1 | Smooth update |
| Skip connection depth‑scale \(\alpha_0\) | 0.5 | Initial skip strength; decays with \(1/\sqrt{\ell}\) |
| Max merge chain per hyperedge | 5 | Rank collapse prevention (Theorem 3) |
| ε‑curriculum start/end | 0.1 → 1.0 | Linear ramp over 50k iterations |
| Optimiser | AdamW, lr=1e-4 | Standard transformer training |
| Hardware | Single A100 (80 GB) | Sufficient for prototype |

**Memory Scaling.** The space complexity is \(O(|\mathcal{V}|d + |\mathcal{E}|d^2 + |\mathcal{E}|\cdot\text{avg. hyperedge size})\). With the above limits and \(d=768\), the hypergraph occupies roughly 2.4 GB, well within GPU memory.

