### 7. Related Work and Novelty Statement

We stand on three pillars: (1) AP schemes for kinetic equations (Jin et al., 2023) — we transfer the AP philosophy to memory management; (2) hypergraph‑augmented Transformers (Qu et al., 2023) — we extend static hypergraphs to dynamic, evolving ones; (3) diffusion‑based attention — we unify it with standard attention through an AP parameter. The novel contribution is the combination of these elements with rigorous error bounds and a stable numerical recipe.

---

### 8. Conclusion and Next Steps

We have provided a self‑contained, mathematically verified blueprint for AP‑HyMem. Theorems 1–3 guarantee stability, consistency, and controlled rank behavior. Algorithms 1–3 translate these guarantees into code. The immediate next step is to implement the prototype on a synthetic regime‑transition benchmark and confirm that the AP loss indeed smooths the \(\varepsilon\)‑performance curve. Subsequent work will scale to billion‑parameter models and integrate with retrieval‑augmented generation.

